		}
		{
			description: [
				"While I had not joined any of the older sanguine factions, I had contacts within each. Those acquaintances may no logner prove useful. I should try to find knowledge left behind by the members of these factions."
				""
				"This old family relic, the Sanguine Blood Charm is powerful in its own right. It empowers my strikes with significant force. But it has another special property. It can be used in the stead of the fateful core ingredient for the special relics of other factions. "
			]
			disable_toast: true
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			id: "71FEEA1CF45FCE10"
			invisible: true
			rewards: [{
				id: "44B6E0CC2250E89D"
				type: "xp_levels"
				xp_levels: 1
			}]
			subtitle: "Sanguine Blood Charm"
			tasks: [{
				id: "40DD44E7499EFBF2"
				item: "desecratedcore:exile_key_item"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Noble Exile"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 8.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["71FEEA1CF45FCE10"]
			description: [
				"The Sanguines of Vine are friends of nature, They harness elemental powers, especially of earth, grow various mystical herbs and commit themselves to astral rituals. I've heard of some powerful natural weapons they are able to uniquely produce. "
				""
				"Higher ranked members even begin to delve into harnessing the power of the colours throughout the world, hidden to most."
			]
			disable_toast: true
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			id: "75BA4B7290E1DA00"
			rewards: [{
				id: "5354A5C3532AEDEC"
				type: "xp_levels"
				xp_levels: 1
			}]
			subtitle: "Vine Amulet"
			tasks: [{
				id: "27053741C5223121"
				item: "desecratedcore:vine_key_item"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Sanguine of Vine"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 9.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["71FEEA1CF45FCE10"]
			description: ["Sanguines of Iron retreat to their workshops to forge powerful weapons, usually staying true to one weapon their whole lives, continually tinkering and improving it. They are master artisans who can produce plenty of specialized tools and equipment."]
			disable_toast: true
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			id: "2139C028FEBE8500"
			rewards: [{
				id: "33606F1F9F7ABF41"
				type: "xp_levels"
				xp_levels: 1
			}]
			subtitle: "Darkstone Ring"
			tasks: [{
				id: "395989B7E42FBDA2"
				item: "desecratedcore:iron_key_item"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Sanguine of Iron"
			x: 1.0d
			y: 10.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["71FEEA1CF45FCE10"]
			description: [
				"The Spectral Artificers create fascinating gadgets and tools that range from most useful to most useless, both technological and magical in nature. I've heard that during the fall of Red Barar, the Spectral Artificers and the Scholars of Yore, specialized in high sorcery, magic circles and enchanting, have merged together and gone underground."
				""
				"Higher ranked Spectral Artificers become powerful reliquerers, gathering relics to craft mighty artefacts and enter the realm of Rifled Spellcasting."
			]
			disable_toast: true
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			id: "04E0E5A8D3613D91"
			rewards: [{
				id: "3D03F1CE4950724E"
				type: "xp_levels"
				xp_levels: 1
			}]
			subtitle: "Spectral Feather"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2F6214FC32F1CE77"
				item: "desecratedcore:artificer_key_item"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Spectral Artificer"
			x: 3.0d
			y: 10.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["71FEEA1CF45FCE10"]
			description: [
				"The Cultist Moon faction had faced a severe collapse even before the collapse of sanguine society. They adhered to the wider Tarot system used more widely by the other continents, claiming the Moon Arcana as their own. Suddenly, they became unable to craft Moon Tarot cards as they could before with ease, putting a stop to their power. Without the stored knowledge in the tarot cards, they stagnated. Eventually, they became able to make Inverted version of their regular tarot cards, but with twisted effects."
				""
				"The Moon faction still widely utilizes blood magic, but I might have to go on a journey to find traces of them."
			]
			disable_toast: true
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			id: "3B6BAB7182971A38"
			rewards: [{
				id: "10514781DB08653E"
				type: "xp_levels"
				xp_levels: 1
			}]
			subtitle: "Tarot: The Moon"
			tasks: [{
				id: "40A1B80F22D3CCCF"
				item: "desecratedcore:moon_key_item"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Cultists of the Moon"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 9.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"I have heard from my former Spectral Artificer friends about enchanting. It is a most powerful way of enhancing tools, weapons and armour. Unfortunately, my knowledge may be lacking, I can only make use of some weaker enchantments."
				""
				"&a(Enchanting is overhauled and you cannot enchant normally anymore. Enchantments require specific recipes instead of luck and absurd amounts of experience. Spectral Artificers can make the most out of enchanting. Relics replace Unbreaking, Sharpness, Protection and Efficiency.)"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"&4You should find a Spectral Artificer's library and feed it to me."
				""
				"You eat books? Well, I'll see if I can satiate you one day."
				""
				"&4Sanguine enchanting methods differ from the humans in the north. You should still be able to find plenty of enchanted relics in ruins around the country. You do know about relics, yes?"
				""
				"Yes, they can infuse tools with superior durability, effiency or power."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&4You should be able to borrow the properties of amethyst to infuse rudimentary relic onto tools. You can combine any dormant relic with an infusion smithing template onto a tool to imbue it with more efficiency, durability, protection, speed or magic capacity."
				""
				"&4With an enchanting table made from copper and diamonds, you will be able to obtain common enchantments, but not anything particularly more advanced."
			]
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			icon: "ascendant_arcana:copper_enchanting_table"
			id: "2769096977DA8528"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "03DCD0AB5EF88A8C"
					item: {
						Count: 1
						id: "ftbquests:lootcrate"
						tag: {
